<para id="X39400000QY01GC" category="C" type-id="302Z1" name-id="0659Q-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P0011/59</dtccode>
<dtcname>VVT Control (Advance Malfunction)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0012/59</dtccode>
<dtcname>VVT Control (Retard Malfunction)</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000QY01GC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002T600000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>This VVT system controls the intake camshaft to provide the optimal valve timing for each driving condition. This control is performed based on conditions such as intake air volume, throttle position and engine coolant temperature. Based on the signals from these sensors, the engine control computer adjusts the oil control valve; as a result, the relative position of the camshaft is optimized, improving engine torque and fuel economy and reducing exhaust emissions. The engine control computer also detects the actual valve timing using the signal from the camshaft position sensor and performs feedback control to achieve the target valve timing.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A145886J04" width="7.106578999in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
<ptxt/>
</item>
</list1>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="0.86in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="3.25in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="2.97in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTCNo.</ptxt>
<ptxt>SAE/TCCS</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>1. Detection condition 2. Malfunction status 3. Malfunction duration 4. Other</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
